# check-gated-layout-macros.allowlist
# Acknowledged partial-coverage layout-macro guards. Format: "header:MACRO".
# One entry per line; text after '#' is a comment. Add an entry ONLY with a
# justification and after MANUAL layout analysis. See
# docs/render-backend-seams/gated-layout-macro-guard.md.

# VULKAN-EDGE-FOG-ISLAND-2a/2b (fix 9cce8e68). MC2_VULKAN_ISLAND adds the
# trailing-ish member vkFogIsland_ + method decls to gosPostProcess. The define
# is now PUBLIC on gameos and PRIVATE on gameos_main + mc2 (the TUs the fix
# scoped). It is NOT propagated to the other linked consumers (mclib,
# renderworld, gameadapters, gui_runtime) because they do not link gameos, and
# is absent from the editor build entirely. ACCEPTED because:
#   (1) the option ships default-OFF -> in every shipped build the member is
#       absent in ALL TUs, so the layout is uniform (this is the byte-identical
#       default-OFF contract). The residual is latent, ON-only.
#   (2) when turned ON for the island bring-up build, the fix covers the TUs
#       that actually construct/serialize gosPostProcess and access it directly.
# RESIDUAL RISK (documented, not hidden): with the option ON, inline accessors
# in gos_postprocess.h that read members declared AFTER vkFogIsland_ (getWidth/
# getHeight etc.) compiled in a non-gameos consumer TU would see a shifted
# offset. Correct long-term fix = move vkFogIsland_ behind a pImpl, OR make the
# define reach every consuming target. Tracked as a follow-up, not a blocker
# for the default-OFF ship.
GameOS/gameos/gos_postprocess.h:MC2_VULKAN_ISLAND
